From: Baptiste Faisy <baptiste.faisy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] product-mini/linux: do not link -ldl/-lpthread on QNX

QNX provides pthreads and dlopen() inside libc: the SDP 8.0 target ships no
libpthread and no libdl, so linking them fails with

    ld: cannot find -ldl
    ld: cannot find -lpthread

Keep the existing link line everywhere else and drop those two flags when
CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME is QNX. -lm is retained: QNX does ship libm.so.3.

Verified with SDP 8.0 (qcc 12.2.0, -Vgcc_ntox86_64): the interpreter links
and produces an ELF PIE with interpreter /usr/lib/ldqnx-64.so.2, needing only
libm.so.3, libc.so.6 and libgcc_s.so.1.

Applies to WAMR-2.4.5 (commit 25bd7eb63e828e4bd242cc9b38d260b4b31c6605).
diff --git a/product-mini/platforms/linux/CMakeLists.txt b/product-mini/platforms/linux/CMakeLists.txt
index cef8329..4b2a5d2 100644
--- a/product-mini/platforms/linux/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/product-mini/platforms/linux/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -192,7 +192,12 @@ set_target_properties (vmlib PROPERTIES
   POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON
 )
 
-target_link_libraries (vmlib ${LLVM_AVAILABLE_LIBS} ${UV_A_LIBS} -lm -ldl -lpthread)
+if (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "QNX")
+  # QNX provides pthreads and dlopen() inside libc: there is no libpthread nor libdl.
+  target_link_libraries (vmlib ${LLVM_AVAILABLE_LIBS} ${UV_A_LIBS} -lm)
+else ()
+  target_link_libraries (vmlib ${LLVM_AVAILABLE_LIBS} ${UV_A_LIBS} -lm -ldl -lpthread)
+endif ()
 
 install (TARGETS vmlib
   EXPORT iwasmTargets
